I've fixed the red CI on main, and it's committed as b34ab98e. All checks pass locally; GitHub CI hasn't run on the commit yet.

Cause: yoyo --print-system-prompt exited 1 with "No API key found" when no key was set. That blocked anyone just inspecting their prompt, and it's why two config_fifo tests failed in CI. They passed on the evolve runner only because the test helper inherited that runner's ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.

What changed:
• `src/cli.rs`: with --print-system-prompt, a missing key now gets the same "not-needed" placeholder that ollama/custom already use. The key is never sent, because the process prints the prompt and exits. -p, the REPL, --print and everything else still fail with the same message. The edit adds 3 lines, which keeps the file inside the module-size gate's grace band.
• `tests/config_fifo.rs`: the test helper run_yoyo_env now strips every inherited API_KEY / *_API_KEY before applying the test's own variables. Tests that set a key on purpose still get it.
  • Once the helper stopped inheriting keys, CI's failure showed up on this runner too, even though it has a key.
  • New test print_system_prompt_needs_no_api_key, plus a near-miss test prompt_mode_without_key_still_refuses that checks -p hi with no key still refuses.
• Docs: one sentence in docs/src/configuration/system-prompts.md saying the flag works without an API key.

Verification:
• env -u ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -u API_KEY cargo test --test config_fifo gives 12 passed (it was 9 passed / 3 failed before the fix).
• Positive control: I reverted cli.rs to HEAD, ran the tests and restored the fix in one step. The same 3 tests failed, including the new one, and cli.rs is back to the fix with no marker left in it.
• cargo fmt --check, clippy with -D warnings, cargo build and the full cargo test all pass, with 0 failures.

The commit also includes .yoyo/risk_weights.json, which already had uncommitted changes before I started; the instructed git add -A picked it up.
